<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Holstein</h1><p class="st-meta">1474 CE – 1864 CE · capital Glückstadt</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A German duchy ruled by the kings of Denmark for four centuries, whose bond with Schleswig sparked two 19th-century wars.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1460 the estates of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-schleswig">Duchy of Schleswig</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-holstein">County of Holstein</a> elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-i-of-denmark">King Christian I of Denmark</a> as their ruler, promising that the lands would remain 'forever undivided'. In 1474 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-holy-roman-emperor">Emperor Frederick III</a> raised Holstein, a fief of the empire, to a duchy.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-holstein">Holstein</a> was governed together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig">Schleswig</a>, but while Schleswig was a Danish fief, Holstein belonged to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> and later the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/german-confederation">German Confederation</a>. From 1544 it was split between the royal line and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-holstein-gottorp">Duchy of Holstein-Gottorp</a>, with their lands intermingled. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gluckstadt">Glückstadt</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-iv-of-denmark">Christian IV</a> in 1617, became the seat of royal government. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a> took hold in the 16th century.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Danish attempts to tie <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig">Schleswig</a> more closely to the kingdom led to war in 1848 to 1851 and again in 1864, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-holstein">Holstein</a> came under Austrian administration in 1865 and was annexed by Prussia in 1866, becoming part of the province of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/provisional-government-of-schleswig-holstein">Schleswig-Holstein</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-holstein.jpg" alt="Duchy of Holstein" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Sir Iain · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Merchant_Ensign_of_Holstein-Gottorp_(Lions_sinister).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1474 CE – 1864 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Glückstadt</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Christian I, Christian IV, Frederick VI</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Low German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Herzogtum Holstein</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1669&amp;focus=duchy-of-holstein" aria-label="Duchy of Holstein on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4889 330 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Holstein lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5209 586L5214 576M5209 586L5218 590M5209 586L5229 694M5209 586L5274 535M5209 586L5199 691M5209 586L5300 622M5209 586L5211 567M5209 586L5274 535M5209 586L5211 567"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5214 576h0M5218 590h0M5229 694h0M5274 535h0M5199 691h0M5300 622h0M5211 567h0M5274 535h0M5211 567h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5209 586h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5209 586h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Glückstadt. <a href="/atlas?year=1669&amp;focus=duchy-of-holstein">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
